to the MMD statistic, with a similar effect. The
two effects compose: a small budget can be spent
either as more templates with fewer samples or
fewer templates with more samples. The K = 20,
N = 50 configuration reaches 100% on the 36-
model set and matches MET and RUT on identity
discrimination. Type-I error remains controlled
across the entire grid: only 1 of 36 models is falsely
rejected at a single cell (K=10, N=10), with all
other cells at 0/36 (Appendix Table 13).
Budget estimate.
A full audit at K = 20, N =
50 costs 1,000 queries per endpoint. A lighter K =
10, N = 50 operating point costs 500 queries and
still reaches 99.84%. At typical API pricing both
points are well under $1 per endpoint.
