4.7
Robustness to Adaptive Providers
We evaluate three adaptive evasion strategies:
prompt-based mimicry, LoRA fine-tuning, and
probabilistic substitution. We also discuss exact
per-probe replay by a fully adaptive provider that
recognizes audit probes.
Prompt-based mimicry. We wrap each substitute
in adversarial system prompts with four knowledge
levels: none, claimed identity, the reference’s ag-
gregate tool-call profile, and few-shot reference
demonstrations from disjoint probes. AgentProv
rejects both substitutes under every condition (Ta-
ble 7), showing that prompt-level mimicry does not
reproduce the reference tool-selection behavior.
